  "manual": {
    "notes": [
      "BIRTH CORRECTED (research 2026-07-03): ~13 Nov 1906 at Whitehaven, Cumberland (the tree's alternate date) — GRO registration Mar quarter 1907, Whitehaven district, vol 10b p. 689; the ONLY Ellen Larkin birth registered in Cumberland 1904-1912, and none exists anywhere in England & Wales Dec 1905-Dec 1906. The '8 Nov 1905' date is refuted as an England birth.",
      "'Hamilton, England' RESOLVED: no such town — Hamilton Terrace / Hamilton Lane are streets in Whitehaven (Corkickle, CA28); a street address on a later US document was promoted to a town name. Not Hamilton, Lanarkshire.",
      "MOTHER: NOT Mary Blackmore (that identity is a five-way merge chimera — see her record). Real mother unknown pending the GRO index lookup (free account: Births Mar Q 1907 Whitehaven 10b/689, mother's-maiden-name column). Candidates: the wife recorded as Mary Ellen Larkin (d. Mar Q 1906 Whitehaven, aged 42 — only possible if that death belongs to another Whitehaven Larkin family) or an unidentified later partner of Thomas (no Thomas Larkin remarriage registered in Cumberland 1906-1911). Her US Social Security application (Ellen Larkin Reagan, 1906-1995 MA) would also give the maiden name.",
      "PROBABLE BROTHER: Samuel Larkin, b. Jun Q 1903, Whitehaven 10b/733 — the only other Larkin birth registered in Whitehaven district 1902-1916.",
      "Orphaned young: father died 1920 in Maine; Ellen sailed to Quebec May 1921 aged ~14, crossed to the US permanently 1929, married Frederick Lewis Reagan most likely in Massachusetts (no Reagan x Larkin in the Maine 1892-1966 index)."
    ],
